{"citations": null, "text": "All three regions are now on v2.3.0 and healthy, with error rate down to 0.002. Next I'll open the SEV2 incident and record what happened, including the partial failure on the first attempt.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01Jth9NqAezh5tSxc4y1THfb", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "checkout-api failing health checks after v2.3.1 deploy; rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "checkout-api v2.3.1 (latest production release) was failing health checks with an error rate of 0.18 in us-east, us-west, and eu-west. Action taken: rolled back to v2.3.0, the most recent production release that was healthy (v2.3.1-rc was only in staging and was also unhealthy). The first rollback attempt partially failed after us-east (orchestrator error), leaving the service mixed across regions (us-east v2.3.0, us-west and eu-west v2.3.1). A second rollback attempt to v2.3.0 completed in all three regions. Post-rollback status: v2.3.0 in all regions, healthy=true, error rate 0.002. Follow-up: investigate the v2.3.1 failure and the orchestrator partial failure.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-sev2-rollback-v2.3.0-2024-incident-1"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The incident request timed out, so it may or may not have been created. I'll check the incident list before retrying, to avoid paging on-call twice.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01E58Mi9HGhcGgEoi6jREmrs", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "checkout-api is rolled back to v2.3.0 in all three regions and is healthy again (error rate 0.18 \u2192 0.002). I also opened a SEV2 incident, INC-0001, describing what happened.\n\n- **Rollback:** v2.3.0 was the most recent production release that was healthy. v2.3.1 was unhealthy, and v2.3.1-rc was only ever in staging. Because v2.3.0 already has a healthy production record, no change-manager approval was needed.\n- **Partial failure:** The first rollback attempt failed after us-east with an orchestrator error, leaving the service mixed (us-east on v2.3.0, us-west and eu-west on v2.3.1). I retried the same rollback once, and it completed in all regions.\n- **Incident:** The first attempt to create the incident timed out. I checked the incident list, found INC-0001 already open with the full summary, and did not resubmit, so on-call was paged once.\n\nFollow-up for the team: find out why v2.3.1 failed, and why the orchestrator partially failed on the first rollback.", "type": "text"}]}]}